  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 136 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nUpper ridging over the western Plains moves est tonight, with a\nclosed low moving from southern Saskatchewan into Manitoba and\nOntario by tomorrow. No precip expected in our area with the\nsystem, but winds will shift back around to the south and our\nstratus that is currently trying to scatter out in central ND\nand north central MN will likely fill back in. Cloudy skies for\nmuch of the night should keep temps from falling too much even\nwith light winds, and also keep fog limited to the far western\nedge of the stratus deck. At this point that line seems like it\nwill be mostly over central ND, but will watch the Devils Lake\nBasin in case it gets a bit more clearing than expected\novernight. With cloud cover continuing, raised lows a bit and\nlowered highs for tomorrow, until the upper low moves off to the\nnortheast of us and we get more of a westerly fetch to the wind\nfor Saturday.\n\nNorthwesterly flow aloft sets up for Sunday and continues into\nnext week. There is decent agreement on the ensemble members on\na progressive shortwave moving through on Monday, but they also\nkeep the region dry with probabilities of measurable rain near \nzero. Slightly better chances with another reinforcing shortwave\nWednesday, but still the probability of anything more than a \nfew sprinkles is less than 20 percent. Temps look to be on the \nwarmer side of average.",
